    {
      "id": "s2023-e3-q01",
      "number": 1,
      "points": 8,
      "stem": "Using the 2nd order Taylor polynomial of $f(x) = \\ln(x)$ centered at $a = 3$,\n\n$$\n\\ln(\\pi) \\approx \\ln(3) + \\frac{1}{3}(\\pi - 3) - \\frac{1}{18}(\\pi - 3)^2.\n$$\n\nAccording to the Taylor Remainder Theorem, this approximation has error equal to",
      "choices": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "$\\frac{(\\pi - 3)^3}{6c^3}$ for some $c$ between 3 and $\\pi$"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "$\\frac{(\\pi - 3)^2}{2c^2}$ for some $c$ between 3 and $\\pi$"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "$\\frac{(\\pi - 3)^2}{c^2}$ for some $c$ between 3 and $\\pi$"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "$\\frac{(\\pi - 3)^3}{6c^2}$ for some $c$ between 3 and $\\pi$"
        },
        {
          "label": "E",
          "text": "$\\frac{(\\pi - 3)^3}{3c^3}$ for some $c$ between 3 and $\\pi$"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "E",
      "lessonIds": [
        "L28"
      ],
      "sourcePage": 2,
      "status": "reviewed"
    },
